Writing Tips
A concluding paragraph ends the essay. It
• is usually two to four sentences in length;
• summarises the main points;
• restates the thesis statement in the introduction in different words;
• may give a final thought or feeling;
• may make a prediction;
• may suggest something;
• may share a hope.
